    "The flat roof area(s) of the development to which this permission relates shall not be used as a roof garden, balcony, seating area or other similar amenity area, and shall not be accessed except for the purpose of maintenance or in the case of emergency.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The proposed works are considered to fall within the parameters of  permitted development as set out under Schedule 2, Part 1, Classes A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r",
    "Having regard to the siting, scale, and design of the development, it is considered that the proposal would not give rise to any material overbearing effects, material loss of light, or any material impact to the privacy of neighbours by reason of overlooking in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy, and the guidance set out in the Council's Residential Design SPD (2012) (SPD)."
